`fake.parse('{{ name }}')` first goes through `Faker.__getattribute__`; since `parse` is not a declared attribute on the proxy, lookup falls through to `Faker.__getattr__`. In `__getattr__`, when there are multiple factories (`len(self._factories) > 1`) and the requested attribute is in `generator_attrs`, the proxy raises `NotImplementedError` instead of delegating. `generator_attrs` is built from `dir(Generator)` and therefore includes `parse`, while `Generator.parse` itself is a normal generator method body that would only run if delegation occurred. So the proxy-layer `__getattr__` for `parse` is reached, but `faker.generator.parse` is not.

## Answer
{"faker_generator_parse_reached":false,"faker_proxy_getattr_parse_reached":true}
